window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-9573e00609d9bad8"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"turn-figma-designs-into-code\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"figma\">将 Figma 设计稿转化为代码</h1> <p>根据 Figma 选区和结构化设计背景，实现精致 UI，并进行视觉检查。</p> <p>使用 Codex 从 Figma 获取设计背景、素材和变体，将它们转化为符合代码库设计系统的代码，再通过 Playwright 与 Figma 参考稿比较并迭代，直到效果合适。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>在现有代码库中，根据 Figma 实现已经设计好的界面或流程。</li> <li>希望 Codex 根据结构化设计背景进行开发的团队。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/figma\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">figma（需联网）</a></td> <td>将设计实现为代码，在已发布组件与源文件之间建立 Code Connect 映射，并生成适用于项目的设计系统规则，以便重复使用。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/playwright-interactive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$playwright（需联网）</a></td> <td>在真实浏览器中检查响应式表现并验证实现效果。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"tech-stack-recommendations\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技术栈建议</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>需求</th> <th>建议选择</th> <th>原因</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>设计来源</td> <td><a href=\"https://www.figma.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Figma（需联网）</a></td> <td>使用具体的画板或组件选区，能让实现紧扣设计稿。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>实现符合设计系统的 UI</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请在当前项目中使用 Figma 技能实现这份设计。\n\n要求：\n- 先针对准确的节点或画板调用 `get_design_context`。\n- 如果返回内容被截断，使用 `get_metadata` 梳理文件结构，再只针对需要的节点重新调用 `get_design_context`。\n- 开始编写代码前，针对准确的设计变体运行 `get_screenshot`。\n- 复用现有设计系统组件和设计变量。\n- 将 Figma 输出转换为此代码库正在使用的工具和组件模式，不要另造一套平行体系。\n- 尽量贴合间距、布局、层级和响应式行为。\n- 遵循代码库现有的路由、状态和数据获取模式。\n- 确保页面在桌面端和移动端都能响应式显示。\n- 如果 Figma 返回 localhost 图片或 SVG 来源，请直接使用；不要创建占位内容，也不要新增图标包。\n\n验证：\n- 对照 Figma 参考稿，检查完成后的外观和行为。\n- 使用 Playwright 检查 UI 是否符合参考稿，并根据结果迭代。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">技能</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">模型上下文协议</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"introduction\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">简介</h2> <p>选中准确的 Figma 对象后，Codex 可以把设计稿转化为精致的 UI，同时沿用项目已经建立的模式。</p> <p>借助 Figma 技能，Codex 可以通过 Figma MCP 服务器获取结构化设计背景、变量、素材，以及需要实现的准确变体。</p> <p>借助 Playwright interactive 技能，Codex 可以在真实浏览器中打开应用，将实现效果与 Figma 参考稿比较，并反复调整布局或行为，使结果更接近目标。</p> <p><a id=\"set-up-your-figma-project\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"figma_1\">整理 Figma 项目</h2> <p>Figma 文件越整洁，第一次实现通常就越顺利。为了让设计交接更清楚：</p> <ul> <li>尽可能使用变量或设计令牌，尤其是颜色、字体和间距。</li> <li>为可重复使用的 UI 元素创建组件，不要重复使用互不关联的图层。</li> <li>尽量使用自动布局，避免手动定位。</li> <li>为画板和图层设置清晰名称，以便看出主要界面、状态和变体。</li> <li>尽可能在文件中保留真实图标和图片，这样 Codex 就不必猜测。</li> </ul> <p>这能为 Codex 提供更清晰的结构，帮助它把设计转化为可靠、适合投入生产使用的 UI。</p> <p><a id=\"be-specific\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">明确说明</h2> <p>你对交互模式和预期风格描述得越具体，结果通常越好。</p> <p>如果某个状态、断点或交互很重要，请明确指出。如果文件中有多个相似变体，请告诉 Codex 哪一个才是权威参考。</p> <p>越明确地说明哪些内容必须准确匹配、哪些情况应优先遵循代码库惯例，Codex 就越容易做出合适的取舍。</p> <p><a id=\"prepare-the-design-system\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">准备设计系统</h2> <p>如果目标代码库已经有清晰的组件层，Codex 就能更好地工作。它可以直接使用现有组件和设计系统，而不是从头重建。</p> <p>如果有必要，可以告诉 Codex 要复用哪些基础组件、设计变量存放在哪里，以及项目对按钮、输入框、卡片、字体和图标的标准是什么。</p> <p>请把 Figma MCP 的输出（通常看起来像 React 加 Tailwind）当作结构参考，而不是最终代码风格。让 Codex 将输出转换为项目实际使用的工具、组件封装、颜色体系、字体尺度、间距变量、路由、状态管理和数据获取模式。</p> <p><a id=\"workflow\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">工作流程</h2> <p><a id=\"start-from-a-figma-selection\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"figma_2\">从 Figma 选区开始</h3> <p>复制要实现的准确 Figma 画板、组件或变体链接。Figma MCP 工作流程根据链接定位，因此链接需要指向准确节点，而不是附近的父级画板。</p> <p><a id=\"prompt-codex-to-use-figma\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"codex-figma\">提示 Codex 使用 Figma</h3> <p>第一轮实现应以 Figma 为准。请让 Codex 在开始实现前遵循 Figma MCP 流程。</p> <p>提示词中可以包含：</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">1. Run `get_design_context` for the exact node or frame first.\n2. If the response is too large or truncated, run `get_metadata` to map the file and then re-run `get_design_context` only for the nodes you need.\n3. Run `get_screenshot` for the exact variant being implemented.\n4. Only after both the design context and the exact variant are available, download any required assets and start implementation.\n5. Translate the result into the repo's conventions: reuse existing components, replace raw utility classes with the project's system when possible, and keep spacing, hierarchy, and responsive behavior aligned with the design.\n6. If Figma returns a localhost image or SVG source, use it directly. Do not create placeholders or add a new icon package when the asset is already in the payload.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">1. 首先针对准确的节点或画框运行 `get_design_context`。\n2. 如果响应过大或被截断，运行 `get_metadata` 来了解文件结构，然后只针对所需节点重新运行 `get_design_context`。\n3. 针对正在实现的确切变体运行 `get_screenshot`。\n4. 只有在设计上下文和确切变体都已取得之后，才能下载所需素材并开始实现。\n5. 将结果适配为代码库的约定：复用现有组件，尽可能用项目的样式系统替代原始工具类，并让间距、层级和响应式行为与设计一致。\n6. 如果 Figma 返回 localhost 图片或 SVG 源文件，请直接使用。如果载荷中已经包含素材，不要创建占位内容，也不要添加新的图标包。</div></div> <p>完成第一版实现后，Codex 会使用 Playwright 在真实浏览器中验证 UI，并继续调整尚未匹配的视觉细节和交互。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"turn-figma-designs-into-code\">Turn Figma designs into code</h1> <p>Turn Figma selections into polished UI with structured design context and visual checks.</p> <p>Use Codex to pull design context, assets, and variants from Figma, translate them into code that matches the repo's design system, then use Playwright to compare the implementation to the Figma reference and iterate until it looks right.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Implementing already designed screens or flows from Figma in an existing codebase</li> <li>Teams that want Codex to work from structured design context</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/figma\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">figma (online)</a></td> <td>Implement designs in code, create Code Connect mappings between published components and source files, and generate project-specific design system rules for repeatable Figma-to-code work.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/playwright-interactive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$playwright (online)</a></td> <td>Check responsive behavior and verify the implemented UI in a real browser.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"tech-stack-recommendations\">Tech stack recommendations</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Need</th> <th>Good default</th> <th>Why</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Design source</td> <td><a href=\"https://www.figma.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Figma (online)</a></td> <td>A concrete frame or component selection keeps the implementation grounded.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Implement a Design System-Aware UI</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Implement this Figma design in the current project using the Figma skill.\n\nRequirements:\n- Start with `get_design_context` for the exact node or frame.\n- If the response is truncated, use `get_metadata` to map the file and then re-fetch only the needed nodes with `get_design_context`.\n- Run `get_screenshot` for the exact variant before you start coding.\n- Reuse the existing design system components and tokens.\n- Translate the Figma output into this repo's utilities and component patterns instead of inventing a parallel system.\n- Match spacing, layout, hierarchy, and responsive behavior closely.\n- Respect the repo's routing, state, and data-fetch patterns.\n- Make the page responsive on desktop and mobile.\n- If Figma returns localhost image or SVG sources, use them directly and do not create placeholders or add new icon packages.\n\nValidation:\n- Compare the finished UI against the Figma reference for both look and behavior.\n- Use Playwright to check that the UI matches the reference and iterate as needed until it does.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Skills</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">Model Context Protocol</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"introduction\">Introduction</h2> <p>When you have an exact Figma selection, Codex can turn it into polished UI without ignoring the patterns already established in your project.</p> <p>With the Figma skill, Codex can use the Figma MCP server to pull structured design context, variables, assets, and the exact variant it should implement.</p> <p>With the Playwright interactive skill, Codex can open the app in a real browser, compare the implementation to the Figma reference, and iterate on layout or behavior until the result is closer to the target.</p> <h2 id=\"set-up-your-figma-project\">Set up your Figma project</h2> <p>The cleaner your Figma file is, the better the first implementation will be. To improve the handoff:</p> <ul> <li>Use variables or design tokens wherever possible, especially for colors, typography, and spacing</li> <li>Create components for reusable UI elements instead of repeating detached layers</li> <li>Use auto layout as much as possible instead of manual positioning</li> <li>Keep frame and layer names clear enough that the main screen, state, and variants are obvious</li> <li>Keep real icons and images in the file when possible so Codex does not need to guess</li> </ul> <p>This gives Codex better structure to translate into a robust, production-ready UI.</p> <h2 id=\"be-specific\">Be specific</h2> <p>The more specific you are about the expected interaction patterns and the style you want, the better the result will be.</p> <p>If a state, breakpoint, or interaction matters, call it out. If the file contains multiple close variants, tell Codex which one should be treated as the source of truth.</p> <p>The more explicit you are about what needs to match exactly and where repo conventions should win, the easier it is for Codex to make the right tradeoffs.</p> <h2 id=\"prepare-the-design-system\">Prepare the design system</h2> <p>Codex works best when the target repo already has a clear component layer. Codex can automatically use your existing component and design system instead of recreating them from scratch.</p> <p>If you think it's necessary, specify to Codex which primitives to reuse, where your tokens live, and what the repo considers canonical for buttons, inputs, cards, typography, and icons.</p> <p>Treat the Figma MCP output, which often looks like React plus Tailwind, as a structural reference rather than final code style. Ask Codex to translate that output into the project's actual utilities, component wrappers, color system, typography scale, spacing tokens, routing, state management, and data-fetch patterns.</p> <h2 id=\"workflow\">Workflow</h2> <h3 id=\"start-from-a-figma-selection\">Start from a Figma selection</h3> <p>Copy a link to the exact Figma frame, component, or variant you want implemented. The Figma MCP flow is link-based, so the link needs to point to the exact node you want rather than a nearby parent frame.</p> <h3 id=\"prompt-codex-to-use-figma\">Prompt Codex to use Figma</h3> <p>Figma should drive the first pass. Ask Codex to follow the Figma MCP flow before it starts implementing.</p> <p>Things to include in your prompt:</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">1. Run `get_design_context` for the exact node or frame first.\n2. If the response is too large or truncated, run `get_metadata` to map the file and then re-run `get_design_context` only for the nodes you need.\n3. Run `get_screenshot` for the exact variant being implemented.\n4. Only after both the design context and the exact variant are available, download any required assets and start implementation.\n5. Translate the result into the repo's conventions: reuse existing components, replace raw utility classes with the project's system when possible, and keep spacing, hierarchy, and responsive behavior aligned with the design.\n6. If Figma returns a localhost image or SVG source, use it directly. Do not create placeholders or add a new icon package when the asset is already in the payload.\n</code></pre> <p>Once the first implementation is in place, Codex will use Playwright to verify the UI in a real browser and tighten any remaining visual or interaction mismatches.</p>"};
